<Docs title="Console deployment" description="Configure and operate the AgentGuard OIDC console.">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">OPERATE / CONSOLE</span><h1>A guided control plane.</h1><p>The Next.js console is an operator surface for audit browsing, policy simulation, and admin-only delegation workflows.</p></div>
  <h2>Required configuration</h2><div class="docs-table"><div><b>OIDC</b><span>Issuer, client ID, and client secret are mandatory. The console fails closed with 503 when authentication is incomplete.</span></div><div><b>Session</b><span>Use a persistent random session secret of at least 32 characters. Production sessions use the Redis-compatible shared store; memory mode is development-only. Sessions expire after eight hours and logout revokes the shared record.</span></div><div><b>Roles</b><span>Every authenticated user is a viewer. Only explicitly configured claim values receive the admin role.</span></div><div><b>Shared limits</b><span>Use the Redis-compatible session and rate-limit stores before running multiple console replicas; store failures fail closed.</span></div><div><b>Trusted proxy</b><span>Production requires AGENTGUARD_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1. Set it only when the ingress strips client-supplied X-Forwarded-For and replaces it with one validated client address; this isolates login and mutation rate-limit buckets per client.</span></div></div>
  <h2>Operational boundaries</h2><p>The simulator calls the PDP over HTTP. Audit and delegation routes use the bundled CLI against the mounted policy and audit state. Mount those paths read-only in Kubernetes and provide a persistent delegation signing key; the console returns 503 rather than minting with an ephemeral key.</p>
  <p>Kubernetes uses <code>/api/health/live</code> for process liveness and <code>/api/health/ready</code> for readiness. Readiness checks the auth configuration and both shared Redis-compatible stores with bounded, non-mutating PING requests; external dependency failures remove the pod from service without causing a liveness restart loop.</p>
  <h2>Test before promotion</h2><p>Exercise viewer/admin access, expired sessions, logout, PDP failures, audit failures, rate-limit exhaustion, and inaccessible policy/audit mounts. Put TLS at the ingress and keep the console and PDP Services private.</p>
  <p>See the complete <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/console.md">console operations guide ↗</a> and <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/frontend/README.md">configuration reference ↗</a>.</p>
</Docs>
